# Support

If you discover a bug or have a feature request, please open an **Issue** on GitHub.

When reporting bugs, please include:

- Device model
- ROM version
- Kernel version
- Steps to reproduce the issue
- Recovery logs (if available)
- Kernel logs (if available)

This helps identify and fix problems much faster.

---

# Project Philosophy

GlitchCore-KRNL is developed with the following goals in mind:

- Stability over benchmarks
- Clean and maintainable code
- Daily-driver reliability
- Community-driven improvements
- Open-source development

Every release is tested before being published, but as with any custom kernel, there is always some risk involved.

